+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent sets toolChoice to 'required', which forces Gemini (functionCallingConfig mode ANY) to emit a tool call on every model turn, so after approveRefund returns declined the model cannot write a text reply and instead re-calls approveRefund, keeps calling lookupOrder, or exhausts maxTurns and fails.",
+  "evidence": "src/agents.ts:43 is the only agent with toolChoice 'required' (triage uses 'auto', line 54); node_modules/@genkit-ai/google-genai/src/googleai/gemini.ts:801-806 maps request.toolChoice to functionCallingConfig.mode, and converters.ts:372-374 maps 'required' to FunctionCallingMode.ANY, which forces a function call; the symptoms (fail, re-ask approval, keep working on the order) match a tool-forced loop capped by maxTurns: 6. Changing it to 'auto' lets the model answer in text after a decline; tsc --noEmit passes. The live Gemini run was not executed, so this is confirmed by code reading rather than a reproduced run."
+}
